{"vid":"tMMkScMKtsQ","source":"tMMkScMKtsQ.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0,"txt":"You can't master the American accent"},{"t":2.8,"txt":"without mastering the dark L sound. If"},{"t":6.2,"txt":"you've never heard this term before,"},{"t":8.1,"txt":"dark L, I'm not surprised. If you look"},{"t":11.2,"txt":"these words up in a dictionary, they'll"},{"t":13.6,"txt":"all have the same phonetic symbol for L,"},{"t":16.8,"txt":"but they're not the same sound. These"},{"t":19.2,"txt":"L's are light L's. And these L's are"},{"t":22.6,"txt":"dark L's. They're made completely"},{"t":25.1,"txt":"differently. I'm Rachel and I've been"},{"t":27.7,"txt":"teaching the American accent for over 20"},{"t":30.4,"txt":"years. I've never met a student who"},{"t":33.2,"txt":"naturally had this dark L sound. We've"},{"t":36.2,"txt":"always had to work at it. But when my"},{"t":38.2,"txt":"students master this sound, it brings a"},{"t":40.8,"txt":"truly natural and relaxed quality to"},{"t":43.8,"txt":"their voices. I've developed an"},{"t":46,"txt":"extremely effective method for mastering"},{"t":48.7,"txt":"the American accent. You can learn about"},{"t":51,"txt":"it and sign up for my courses at"},{"t":53.3,"txt":"Rachel's English Academy.com."},{"t":55.7,"txt":"Join over 50,000 students who are now"},{"t":58.5,"txt":"speaking English with confidence."},{"t":61,"txt":"What's the difference between these L's"},{"t":63.6,"txt":"and these? How do you know when to make"},{"t":66.2,"txt":"an L a light L and when to make it a"},{"t":68.1,"txt":"dark L?"},{"t":69.4,"txt":"It has to do with where it comes in the"},{"t":71.4,"txt":"syllable. If it comes before the vowel"},{"t":74.1,"txt":"or diphthong sound, it's a light L."},{"t":76.5,"txt":"When we write the word phonetically,"},{"t":78.5,"txt":"you'll see either a space between"},{"t":80.4,"txt":"syllables or mark like this or this. So"},{"t":83.8,"txt":"remember, you're looking at where the L"},{"t":86.4,"txt":"comes in the syllable. So if it's not at"},{"t":89.3,"txt":"the beginning of the word or the end of"},{"t":91.2,"txt":"the word, you'll have to know how the"},{"t":93.1,"txt":"word is broken up into syllables. Long."},{"t":97.1,"txt":"It's before the ah vowel."},{"t":99.3,"txt":"Believe. It's before the ee vowel."},{"t":102.8,"txt":"Clean. Before the ee vowel. These are"},{"t":105.8,"txt":"all light L's."},{"t":108.2,"txt":"Feel. It comes after the ee."},{"t":111.4,"txt":"Valley. It comes after the ah vowel."},{"t":115.4,"txt":"Example. It comes after the schwa at the"},{"t":118.8,"txt":"end of the word. These are all dark L's."},{"t":122.1,"txt":"The most important thing for you to know"},{"t":125.1,"txt":"about the dark L sound is you don't lift"},{"t":127.8,"txt":"your tongue tip up. This is probably the"},{"t":130.6,"txt":"exact opposite of what you've learned,"},{"t":133.4,"txt":"but what you've learned is the light L."},{"t":136.8,"txt":"Let's compare the light L to the dark L"},{"t":139.2,"txt":"just by listening. I'm going to go back"},{"t":141.4,"txt":"and forth. You can also look at the"},{"t":143.4,"txt":"difference in the mouth position, but"},{"t":145.6,"txt":"focus mainly on what you hear."},{"t":148.8,"txt":"Uh uh uh"},{"t":151.6,"txt":"all"},{"t":152.7,"txt":"all all"},{"t":154.6,"txt":"all"},{"t":159.8,"txt":"So, for the dark L, the tongue tip is"},{"t":162,"txt":"down and the back part of the tongue"},{"t":164.4,"txt":"pushes down and back a little bit"},{"t":166.8,"txt":"narrowing the space here. That makes"},{"t":169.6,"txt":"this dark sound. The pitch is low. The"},{"t":172.7,"txt":"vibration is low here in my chest. Try"},{"t":175.5,"txt":"to imitate this sound right now with me."},{"t":179.6,"txt":"all"},{"t":182.4,"txt":"all all"},{"t":185,"txt":"all"},{"t":187.4,"txt":"The word feel."},{"t":189.7,"txt":"The tongue tip arches in the front for"},{"t":192,"txt":"the E vowel."},{"t":193.8,"txt":"Watch as the tongue lowers in the back."},{"t":197.2,"txt":"Now the tongue is lowered pulling back a"},{"t":199.9,"txt":"little bit in the back."},{"t":202.1,"txt":"It's hard to see because of the lips,"},{"t":204.6,"txt":"but the tip of the tongue is still"},{"t":206.2,"txt":"forward. Notice that the lips are"},{"t":208.6,"txt":"relaxed."},{"t":210.5,"txt":"Let's compare the dark L to the mouth at"},{"t":212.5,"txt":"rest. The tongue tip is down touching"},{"t":215,"txt":"the back of the bottom front teeth and"},{"t":217.3,"txt":"the back part of the tongue is"},{"t":218.7,"txt":"stretching back a bit to make this part"},{"t":221,"txt":"of the throat a little narrower. That"},{"t":223.3,"txt":"creates the dark sound. Jaw doesn't drop"},{"t":225.8,"txt":"much and the lips are relaxed."},{"t":228.5,"txt":"That's an important note. The lips are"},{"t":231,"txt":"relaxed. Some of my students, I'm"},{"t":233.8,"txt":"thinking especially of my Vietnamese"},{"t":236,"txt":"students, want to round the lips. That"},{"t":238.9,"txt":"totally changes the sound. We don't want"},{"t":241.2,"txt":"to do that. email"},{"t":243.8,"txt":"email all all all"},{"t":247,"txt":"Look what happens if I round my lips."},{"t":249.8,"txt":"email"},{"t":253,"txt":"We do not want lip rounding. We want"},{"t":255.9,"txt":"relaxed lips. email all all all"},{"t":261.2,"txt":"You know, this really feels more like a"},{"t":263.3,"txt":"vowel than a consonant."},{"t":265.8,"txt":"all all all"},{"t":269.6,"txt":"I've seen so many students struggle"},{"t":272.1,"txt":"because the habit to lift the tongue tip"},{"t":274.4,"txt":"for the L is so strong. Just practice"},{"t":277.2,"txt":"the dark sound. Feel the tongue tip"},{"t":279.2,"txt":"touching the backs of the bottom front"},{"t":281.2,"txt":"teeth."},{"t":283,"txt":"all"},{"t":284.6,"txt":"all Feel what you have to do to your"},{"t":287.2,"txt":"throat."},{"t":288.8,"txt":"all to get that sound down into your"},{"t":291.9,"txt":"chest."},{"t":293.2,"txt":"all Get really used to that sound. Then,"},{"t":297.2,"txt":"move on to single one-syllable words"},{"t":299.8,"txt":"that end in an L and practice them"},{"t":302,"txt":"slowly. feel"},{"t":304.4,"txt":"call"},{"t":305.8,"txt":"tile"},{"t":307.2,"txt":"bowl"},{"t":308.8,"txt":"fill"},{"t":310.2,"txt":"Notice the up-down shape of stress"},{"t":312.4,"txt":"throughout the word. The dark L part of"},{"t":315.1,"txt":"the word comes at the end as the pitch"},{"t":317.5,"txt":"falls down."},{"t":319.1,"txt":"feel"},{"t":324.2,"txt":"feel When you do it slowly, you can"},{"t":326.9,"txt":"focus on how the tongue moves from the E"},{"t":329.5,"txt":"position to the dark sound. feel"},{"t":336.7,"txt":"by relaxing and then pressing down and"},{"t":338.9,"txt":"back a little bit in the back."},{"t":341.6,"txt":"feel"},{"t":345.6,"txt":"Let me show you what feel sounds like"},{"t":348.3,"txt":"with the wrong L, the light L."},{"t":351.6,"txt":"Feel."},{"t":355.4,"txt":"I go right from the E into flipping the"},{"t":357.9,"txt":"tongue tip up. Feel."},{"t":360.8,"txt":"That's a light L. Feel. Now a dark L."},{"t":365,"txt":"Feel. Oh, oh, oh. The sound and"},{"t":368.3,"txt":"vibration really comes down lower to"},{"t":371,"txt":"bring that dark sound into my chest."},{"t":374,"txt":"Feel."},{"t":377.4,"txt":"Feel. But there's no symbol for this. In"},{"t":380.4,"txt":"the dictionary, you'll see the word like"},{"t":383.4,"txt":"with a light L with this symbol, and"},{"t":385.7,"txt":"you'll see the word feel with the same"},{"t":388.4,"txt":"symbol. But we know that's not right. I"},{"t":391,"txt":"wish there was another symbol in the"},{"t":393,"txt":"International Phonetic Alphabet for the"},{"t":394.9,"txt":"dark L that was used regularly. I don't"},{"t":398,"txt":"know why there isn't one. Other dark L"},{"t":400.6,"txt":"words, pool,"},{"t":402.6,"txt":"smile. The sound itself is tricky to"},{"t":405.5,"txt":"get, but you can get it. Expose yourself"},{"t":408.2,"txt":"to the sound enough times and your body"},{"t":410.8,"txt":"will pick it up. That's exactly what we"},{"t":413.2,"txt":"do in Rachel's English Academy. You get"},{"t":415.6,"txt":"so much exposure and audio training that"},{"t":418.5,"txt":"your body naturally picks it up and"},{"t":420.7,"txt":"makes it a habit. There's one other"},{"t":423,"txt":"tricky thing to know about the dark L."},{"t":425.4,"txt":"You already know tongue tip down. Sounds"},{"t":428.3,"txt":"more like a vowel than a consonant. But"},{"t":431.9,"txt":"what about when the next sound is a"},{"t":434.2,"txt":"vowel? Then after the dark sound, we do"},{"t":437.9,"txt":"lift the tongue tip to separate it from"},{"t":440.1,"txt":"the next vowel. So, dark sound, lift the"},{"t":443.5,"txt":"tongue tip, and connect into the next"},{"t":445.8,"txt":"vowel. Do not leave out the dark sound."},{"t":449.4,"txt":"We know the word feel oh has a dark"},{"t":453.2,"txt":"sound. But let's look at the word"},{"t":455.8,"txt":"feeling."},{"t":457.3,"txt":"The L comes after the E vowel in the"},{"t":459.7,"txt":"first syllable, so it's still a dark L,"},{"t":463,"txt":"but the next sound is a vowel, the"},{"t":465.2,"txt":"beginning of the ing ending. I'm going"},{"t":467.6,"txt":"to say it slowly."},{"t":469.6,"txt":"Feeling."},{"t":477.9,"txt":"I have the F, the E vowel, the dark"},{"t":481.5,"txt":"sound, then I lift my tongue tip and go"},{"t":484,"txt":"into the ing ending. Feeling."},{"t":489.7,"txt":"Feeling."},{"t":492.5,"txt":"Let's look at another example. He fell"},{"t":495,"txt":"in love."},{"t":496.3,"txt":"Fallen."},{"t":502.3,"txt":"F consonant, A sound, dark sound,"},{"t":506.5,"txt":"lifting the tongue tip quickly, and the"},{"t":508.8,"txt":"word in."},{"t":510.3,"txt":"Fallen."},{"t":514.3,"txt":"Fallen. He fell in love. What does it"},{"t":517.4,"txt":"sound like without the dark sound? It"},{"t":519.6,"txt":"sounds like this. Fallen."},{"t":522.4,"txt":"Fallen."},{"t":524.5,"txt":"No dark sound. Fell."},{"t":527.7,"txt":"I want that dark sound. It's so"},{"t":530.2,"txt":"important in American English. Fell."},{"t":533.7,"txt":"Fallen. [snorts]"},{"t":534.9,"txt":"Fallen. He fell in love. I'll say it"},{"t":537.8,"txt":"again."},{"t":538.8,"txt":"If it's a dark L, make that dark sound,"},{"t":541.6,"txt":"ol, even if you're linking into a vowel"},{"t":544.9,"txt":"and need to lift your tongue tip."},{"t":547.1,"txt":"In Rachel's English Academy, I have"},{"t":549,"txt":"students really lock in the dark sound"},{"t":551.8,"txt":"before moving on to this idea of linking"},{"t":554.3,"txt":"into another word."},{"t":556.1,"txt":"Ol is what's most important. Let's work"},{"t":559.5,"txt":"on that one more time. Now, I want you"},{"t":562.2,"txt":"to be repeating out loud with me."},{"t":564.7,"txt":"Ol."},{"t":568.2,"txt":"Feel."},{"t":573.4,"txt":"Fill."},{"t":579,"txt":"smile"},{"t":585.1,"txt":"Great work. Keep your learning going now"},{"t":587.4,"txt":"with this video and don't forget to"},{"t":589.3,"txt":"check out rachelsenglishacademy.com"},{"t":592.2,"txt":"to learn more about the American accent"},{"t":594.4,"txt":"training courses that can help you"},{"t":596.4,"txt":"develop a truly American voice. That's"},{"t":599.5,"txt":"it and thanks so much for using Rachel's"},{"t":602.2,"txt":"English."}],"words":[{"t":0,"w":"You"},{"t":0.4,"w":"can't"},{"t":0.8,"w":"master"},{"t":1.44,"w":"the"},{"t":1.64,"w":"American"},{"t":2.16,"w":"accent"},{"t":2.76,"w":"without"},{"t":3.32,"w":"mastering"},{"t":4.04,"w":"the"},{"t":4.2,"w":"dark"},{"t":4.84,"w":"L"},{"t":5.16,"w":"sound."},{"t":6.04,"w":"If"},{"t":6.24,"w":"you've"},{"t":6.48,"w":"never"},{"t":6.8,"w":"heard"},{"t":7.04,"w":"this"},{"t":7.2,"w":"term"},{"t":7.44,"w":"before,"},{"t":8.12,"w":"dark"},{"t":8.52,"w":"L,"},{"t":8.92,"w":"I'm"},{"t":9.08,"w":"not"},{"t":9.32,"w":"surprised."},{"t":10.4,"w":"If"},{"t":10.68,"w":"you"},{"t":10.84,"w":"look"},{"t":11.2,"w":"these"},{"t":11.6,"w":"words"},{"t":11.92,"w":"up"},{"t":12.12,"w":"in"},{"t":12.24,"w":"a"},{"t